From what I see in the codebase and the difference in deeplinks I would have to introduce a bit more complicated logic into the {{magic-login.html}} on the DP side to support both Android and iOS formats.

{noformat}var search = window.location.search;
if (!search.startsWith("?t=")) {
    search = search.substring(1);
}
window.location.replace('boltdriverapp://magic-login/' + search);{noformat}

And change the android URL in fleet/driver from {{https://bolt.eu/driverapp/magic-login/}} → {{https://partners.bolt.eu/driverapp/magic-login.html?}}

This would add a link {{https://partners.bolt.eu/driverapp/magic-login.html?SOMETOKENVALUEHERE}} to the sent email and the updated {{magic-login.html}} logic will see that it needs to remove the starting {{?}} from the {{window.location.search}}

I can’t see a way how we could do it with only a server change due to the different deep-link functions.

*Future proof solution*

It might be better to add an additional query param that indicated the platform so that we can use that to make the decision in the {{magic-login.html}}

Something like {{https://partners.bolt.eu/driverapp/magic-login.html?platform=iOS&token=SOMETOKENVALUEHERE}}

This way we can have a more intuitive logic in {{magic-login.html}} Might have to check that every other magic-link logic using the same provider would also keep working. Login in the {{magic-login.html}} would have to be backwards compatible with the old logic while the server update has been deployed backwards compatibility can be removed at a later date.

