RCA:

* in general, bug is caused by wrong {{chatID}} value passed into {{ChatProvider.getChat}} , it’s a value of old chat
* there’s a interactor for handling active order called {{RideHailingActiveOrderInteractor}}
* it contains {{_state}} built from {{RideHailingActiveOrderInteractorState}} which contains {{contactOptions}} , with default value {{.idle}}
* interactor is observing active order changes, and when such change happens, it decides to fetch or not {{contactOptions}} if it’s current state is {{.idle}} and {{orderStatus}} it’s in necessary state
* and now we go into “core” of the issue - in the described repro steps, when one driver rejects our order and second driver quickly accepts new order then instance of {{RideHailingActiveOrderInteractor}} is “reused” and  {{contactOptions}} value is not reset to {{.idle}} thus, new contact options aren’t fetched ({{fetchContactOptions}} isn’t called ) -> and that’s the reason of passing wrong {{chatID}} into {{ChatProvider.getChat}}  

So to fix it, in interactor’s {{updateRequestingDrivers}} is to update {{contactOption}} value.

Fix is waiting for a review now.

